<title>AUSTRALIA: British Airways starts Brisbane-UK flights.</title>
<headline>British Airways starts Brisbane-UK flights.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Thursday it will introduce five direct flights a week from the Queensland state capital of Brisbane to London from October 27.</p>
<p>The service, which will include a single stop in Singapore, would cut three hours off the total flying time and replace the current Brisbane/Sydney/Bangkok/London route, BA said.</p>
<p>It said all BA flights from Brisbane would be a 'same plane' service, making it the only airline to offer a same plane service to London from Brisbane.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
